From 8f09fa43c29a09ba58e45a0f8874045eb9f8e6fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aression <lvdifine@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:34:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(trainer): add Score Centering drift correction for
 off-policy RL

Implement additive Score Centering (SC) correction from
arXiv:2609.20807. When enabled via use_score_centering=True, the
actor loss switches from the PPO clipped surrogate to REINFORCE+SC
(pure policy gradient plus an additive drift correction).

Key changes:
- Add score_centering.py: chunked top-k logprob gather and
  correction computation with memory-bounded fp32 workspace
- Add SC config fields to PPOActorConfig with fail-fast
  validation (sc_mode, sc_clip_*, sc_reinforce_baseline)
- Add SC loss path in grpo_loss_fn (REINFORCE+SC and pure
  REINFORCE baseline for fair A/B comparison)
- Propagate sampler top-k logprobs end-to-end: vLLM ->
  io_struct -> remote_inf_engine -> rlvr/types -> actor
- Handle -inf padding for logprob tensors in data pipeline
- Inject trainer logits into loss_fn input for SC when enabled
- Fail fast when the injected logits would be sharded
  (Ulysses/context parallel, tensor-parallel vocab head) and when
  importance_sampling is combined with sc_loss_mode='reinforce'
